// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard user button.
// pins_arduino.h declares this pin as the board's built-in key alias.
// Espressif's own arduino-esp32 variant source for this board (fetched
// directly from GitHub) matches this repo's local file byte-for-byte.
// Independent hardware sources (CNX Software write-up on the ESP32-T/eBox
// module used by Widora boards, plus general Widora AIR product
// descriptions) confirm the physical board carries two onboard buttons -
// a reset button and a separate user button - and two onboard LEDs,
// consistent with a real, physically-present user push-button on this pin
// (also a standard ESP32 strapping pin, matching the existing pinNotes
// entry for GPIO0 inherited from the chip-level default).
// pfodWeb NOTE: alias-collision check performed per audit playbook -
// none of this board's SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/TX/RX alias assignments
// point at GPIO0, so build_boards.js's unconditional bus-capability
// appends do not contaminate the button tag here. No pins_arduino.h edit
// was needed for this board.
